I have a number of standards that I use when writing Docker Compose files:

- Always declare a container_name equal to the name of the Compose service.
- For services with several containers, name them as `<service name>_<subname>`, e.g. `nextcloud_db`
- Always use `restart: 'unless-stopped'`
- Attach containers to the network `web` unless otherwise instructed. Include a basic declaration for this network in the compose file (no need to declare it as external).
- If a service requires multiple containers with networking, create a new network with the service name as its name.
- I use Ansible to template out the files, so use the template `{{ app_root }}` as needed to specify the directory in which volumes are bound. For example, Jellyfin might include the following:
```
    volumes:
      - "{{ app_root }}/jellyfin/config:/config"
```
- If you need to reference the URL at which a service will be accessible, use <service name>.{{ tertiary_domain }}
- Set the timezone to {{ timezone }}
- Declare environment variables using `key: value` syntax, not `- key=value`
- If the project provides env vars to disable telemetry/statistics/etc, include them.
- If the app is to be accessed via the web, I use Traefik as a reverse proxy, so set up labels similar to the below example:
```
    labels:
      traefik.enable: true
      traefik.http.routers.media.rule: Host(`media.{{ tertiary_domain }}`)
      traefik.http.routers.media.tls.certresolver: default
      traefik.http.services.media.loadbalancer.server.port: 8096
```
- Because Traefik is handing TLS termination, if an app provides a TLS endpoint in addition to HTTP, point Traefik to the HTTP endpoint.
- I use Homepage with Docker label support, so add those as well (I prefer to use the name as the description and vice versa). Put it in the group "Apps".


Here's an example of a well-formatted reference Compose file:
```
networks:
  web:

services:
  beaverhabits:
    container_name: beaverhabits
    image: daya0576/beaverhabits:latest
    restart: unless-stopped
    user: 4013:4013

    networks:
      web:

    environment:
      MAX_USER_COUNT: 1
      ENABLE_IOS_STANDALONE: true
      HABITS_STORAGE: DATABASE
      INDEX_SHOW_HABIT_COUNT: true

    volumes:
      - "{{ app_root }}/beaverhabits:/app/.user/"

    labels:
      traefik.enable: true
      traefik.http.routers.habits.rule: Host(`habits.{{ tertiary_domain }}`)
      traefik.http.routers.habits.tls.certresolver: default
      traefik.http.services.habits.loadbalancer.server.port: 8080
      homepage.group: Apps
      homepage.name: Habit tracking
      homepage.icon: beaverhabits.png
      homepage.href: https://habits.{{ tertiary_domain }}/
      homepage.weight: 17
      homepage.description: Beaver Habits
      homepage.siteMonitor: http://beaverhabits:8945
```
